WEBVTT

00:36.862 --> 00:38.480
[Episode 7]
Hey, Mr. Kim.

00:39.510 --> 00:40.866
Jeez.

00:40.866 --> 00:42.827
Running a business for a day or two?
Huh? Don't worry.

00:42.827 --> 00:45.028
- Buy me a drink.
- Guys!

00:46.956 --> 00:49.375
Wait a second. What's going on?

00:49.375 --> 00:52.545
There's no time, so I'll keep it brief.

00:52.545 --> 00:55.965
Important goods are coming
from China tomorrow night, right?

00:55.965 --> 00:59.135
We need to modify that shipment a bit.

00:59.135 --> 01:03.014
So let us borrow your place for two days.

01:03.014 --> 01:05.224
A kind of venue sponsorship.

01:05.224 --> 01:06.710
I think you can just think of it that way.

01:06.710 --> 01:11.939
What are these thugs rambling about?

01:11.939 --> 01:15.040
What are you waiting for? Get them!

01:19.155 --> 01:21.782
- Aren't you going to fight?
- Me alone? What about you?

01:21.782 --> 01:25.444
- Are you scared?
- Scared? You think I'm like you?

01:44.110 --> 01:45.548
Darn it.

02:18.422 --> 02:21.374
I'll kill you, darn it.

02:27.598 --> 02:29.132
Huh?

02:34.021 --> 02:35.722
Come on!

02:50.830 --> 02:52.581
What's it gonna be?

02:52.581 --> 02:54.324
Are you going to lend it to us?

02:58.504 --> 02:59.547
- Ow, my butt.
- Oh, jeez,

02:59.547 --> 03:01.006
it's dusty in here.

03:01.006 --> 03:02.760
If you wanted to help,
you should've stepped in earlier.

03:02.760 --> 03:04.343
You took all the credit for yourself.

03:04.343 --> 03:05.928
You can't even handle seven people?

03:05.928 --> 03:08.055
I was going to do it all by myself,
but you interfered.

03:08.055 --> 03:10.057
You'd be dead if it weren't for me.

03:10.057 --> 03:12.551
No, you'd be dead if it weren't for me.

03:13.811 --> 03:16.856
Yeah, Seong Wo. Location secured.

03:16.856 --> 03:20.225
Let's get into the setup now.

03:20.225 --> 03:21.360
Darn it.

03:21.360 --> 03:22.778
Hey, why are you covered in so much dust?

03:22.778 --> 03:25.063
- Knock it off!
- You really are covered in dust.

03:26.532 --> 03:28.909
Since we'll be working together from now on,

03:28.909 --> 03:30.369
I'll speak comfortably.

03:30.369 --> 03:33.664
- That's okay, right?
- Sure, speak however you like.

03:33.664 --> 03:35.958
I like that attitude.

03:35.958 --> 03:39.786
First, try driving this.

03:41.505 --> 03:43.174
- This?
- Yeah, why not?

03:43.174 --> 03:46.001
It's small enough. Doesn't look that hard.

03:47.553 --> 03:49.972
What are you going to do
while I'm driving it?

03:49.972 --> 03:53.508
I will... do that.

03:58.355 --> 04:00.649
- Start the engine.
- The engine...

04:00.649 --> 04:04.862
That's right. And then,
now push that lever forward.

04:04.862 --> 04:05.988
That's it, alright.

04:05.988 --> 04:08.365
There you go. It's okay, it's okay.

04:08.365 --> 04:11.035
- Can I go now?
- Yeah, step on it steadily.

04:11.035 --> 04:13.412
- Isn't the sound too loud?
- No, keep going at this speed.

04:13.412 --> 04:15.915
- Isn't it too fast?
- Just watch this carefully.

04:15.915 --> 04:18.918
- It's big, no? Now slow down and turn left.
- Okay.

04:18.918 --> 04:20.619
Left turn?

04:38.521 --> 04:40.189
That's correct.

04:40.189 --> 04:42.390
That's correct.

05:07.550 --> 05:09.251
Let me feel it.

05:14.306 --> 05:16.007
This...

05:17.852 --> 05:20.062
- Which mask are you going to wear?
- What?

05:20.062 --> 05:22.347
I'm going with this one.

05:25.025 --> 05:26.527
We need to lure them in.

05:26.527 --> 05:28.320
We'll be drawing everyone this way.

05:28.320 --> 05:29.405
You have to raise it
at exactly the right moment.

05:29.405 --> 05:31.991
Including the Chinese crew,
there'll be a lot of them.

05:31.991 --> 05:35.193
What's the key? The timing.

05:36.912 --> 05:38.414
Everything ready, huh?

05:38.414 --> 05:39.915
Yes, it's perfect.

05:39.915 --> 05:42.459
Man, it's been forever
since our last operation.

05:42.459 --> 05:45.078
My heart's pounding already.

05:45.880 --> 05:48.132
Looks like we're all set,

05:48.132 --> 05:49.592
- so let's go eat.
- What?

05:49.592 --> 05:52.261
You can eat with something this big
coming up?

05:52.261 --> 05:56.223
I'm saying it because of you.
You're so scrawny you got your butt kicked.

05:56.223 --> 05:58.133
I'll make sure you're well nourished.

05:59.393 --> 06:02.104
- You got any money?
- You should pay.

06:02.104 --> 06:04.180
- You're the oldest one here, aren't you?
- Ah.

06:04.180 --> 06:07.336
[Kkuseokji Korean Beef]

06:17.062 --> 06:18.791
Oh, that looks amazing.

06:31.175 --> 06:33.218
Slow down.

06:33.218 --> 06:34.803
Doesn't your boss even buy you meat?

06:34.803 --> 06:38.974
I've been living
on expired convenience-store lunches,

06:38.974 --> 06:40.017
so this tastes incredible.

06:40.017 --> 06:43.228
Indeed, Korean beef
really is on another level.

06:43.228 --> 06:45.022
You only fed him expired food?

06:45.022 --> 06:46.732
Sounds like a real slave driver.

06:46.732 --> 06:48.484
Who are you calling a slave driver?

06:48.484 --> 06:50.861
When did I ever feed you that, you punk?

06:50.861 --> 06:53.322
Every day, and always the least popular ones.

06:53.322 --> 06:54.990
I gave you other things too.

06:54.990 --> 06:58.786
No matter how rough your world is,
you should at least

06:58.786 --> 07:01.080
buy a growing young man
some beef once in a while.

07:01.080 --> 07:04.375
Have some bibimbap and noodles with it.
It tastes even better together.

07:04.375 --> 07:06.335
- Really? Is it okay?
- Of course.

07:06.335 --> 07:09.088
Then I'm gonna eat
until I'm completely stuffed.

07:09.088 --> 07:11.465
Anyone listening would think
I never bought you anything.

07:11.465 --> 07:14.093
We were too busy running that store
with just the two of us.

07:14.093 --> 07:16.971
It was so demanding, we didn't have time.

07:16.971 --> 07:21.767
Besides, I haven't had much beef myself.

07:21.767 --> 07:25.512
By the way, why did you work so hard
at the convenience store?

07:26.397 --> 07:29.108
Well, since he worked hard,
I just followed along and worked hard too.

07:29.108 --> 07:30.985
Do you really need a reason to work hard?

07:30.985 --> 07:36.115
I heard you even won some kind of
Friendly Convenience Store award.

07:36.115 --> 07:38.492
Maybe it suits you better
than being a gangster, huh?

07:38.492 --> 07:39.910
What are you talking about?

07:39.910 --> 07:42.705
Boss, you're perfectly suited to be
the Hwasan faction's second-in-command.

07:42.705 --> 07:44.498
Right now, it's all about
avenging our leader,

07:44.498 --> 07:46.083
so he's being patient, isn't that right?

07:46.083 --> 07:48.168
- Yeah, that's it.
- But still...

07:48.168 --> 07:52.673
Still, being friendly and all? A gangster?

07:52.673 --> 07:53.799
What's wrong with a gangster being friendly?

07:53.799 --> 07:55.801
I guess it's not impossible.

07:55.801 --> 08:00.472
Jeong Ho Myung survived ten years
by staying undercover.

08:00.472 --> 08:02.641
What do you mean by undercover?

08:02.641 --> 08:05.936
Mr. Jeong, be honest with us.

08:05.936 --> 08:08.272
Did you really marry your wife for love?

08:08.272 --> 08:12.526
I mean, we saw you get married
and even have a kid.

08:12.526 --> 08:13.777
But it was hard to believe.

08:13.777 --> 08:16.488
In movies, undercover agents even get married

08:16.488 --> 08:19.199
to maintain their cover, right?

08:19.199 --> 08:20.784
Oh!

08:20.784 --> 08:23.287
Mr. Cho, did you order him to get married?

08:23.287 --> 08:25.914
Why would I give him orders to get married?

08:25.914 --> 08:27.499
You've been watching too many movies.

08:27.499 --> 08:28.751
No, no, that's not what I mean.

08:28.751 --> 08:32.379
I mean, there's a limit
to how much a man can be henpecked.

08:32.379 --> 08:35.466
But Mr. Jeong is completely
under his wife's thumb.

08:35.466 --> 08:37.426
Seriously? So that's what you're really like?

08:37.426 --> 08:40.054
You little punks, what do you take me for?

08:40.054 --> 08:43.047
You got married undercover
to infiltrate that Chinese restaurant, right?

08:43.932 --> 08:45.884
Stop eating!

08:46.685 --> 08:49.188
I buy you expensive beef,
and this is what I get?

08:49.188 --> 08:50.397
- What are you doing?
- What's gotten into you?

08:50.397 --> 08:52.107
- Just eat the soybean paste stew, you fool.
- Don't act like this in front of food.

08:52.107 --> 08:54.818
- I said don't eat!
- Alright, alright.

08:54.818 --> 08:57.654
And what's so expensive about it?
I checked the menu on the way in.

08:57.654 --> 09:00.199
It won't cost that much.
Order whatever you want.

09:00.199 --> 09:02.367
And why are you making a fuss?
We can handle ourselves.

09:02.367 --> 09:03.577
- Really?
- Order more.

09:03.577 --> 09:06.404
Ma'am! Another round of beef, please!

09:07.664 --> 09:10.116
Look at how generous this is.

09:14.630 --> 09:16.331
What are you doing?

09:23.180 --> 09:25.340
I've got a lot on my mind now.

09:26.809 --> 09:31.021
Like you said, I've spent ten years
running a convenience store.

09:31.021 --> 09:34.599
Makes me wonder
if I can still pull off an operation.

09:36.151 --> 09:38.362
Getting cold feet again?

09:38.362 --> 09:40.697
Why do you keep saying I'm scared?

09:40.697 --> 09:43.450
Do you really think I'd be scared
of that punk In Goo?

09:43.450 --> 09:46.578
It's just that there are a lot of them.

09:46.578 --> 09:51.250
And I'm not exactly in top shape.
I underestimated them before and paid for it.

09:51.250 --> 09:56.913
Makes me wonder if I'm really past my prime.

09:58.674 --> 10:02.719
But you're not worried at all?

10:02.719 --> 10:06.756
You think your body's still
what it was ten years ago?

10:08.350 --> 10:11.270
If I were the same as ten years ago,

10:11.270 --> 10:13.638
do you think I'd be working with you guys?

10:15.441 --> 10:17.025
There's nothing to be scared of.

10:17.025 --> 10:18.986
My calculations are never wrong.

10:18.986 --> 10:21.697
With you, Ma Gong Bok, Seong Wo, and me.

10:21.697 --> 10:25.117
We're not washed up enough
to lose to someone like Yoo In Goo.

10:25.117 --> 10:28.370
So don't worry needlessly.

10:28.370 --> 10:30.697
Just follow the route I planned.

10:31.415 --> 10:34.585
Then you won't end up
getting beaten up alone.

10:34.585 --> 10:36.420
Oh, dear.

10:36.420 --> 10:39.214
Now, this finally feels like a real alliance.

10:39.214 --> 10:41.633
Well, we've come this far.

10:41.633 --> 10:43.710
I'll trust you this once.

10:44.676 --> 10:46.667
Jeez, seriously.

11:05.532 --> 11:07.483
You guys go in first.

11:08.702 --> 11:10.829
Why? Aren't you coming?

11:10.829 --> 11:13.123
I thought we were doing one last check.

11:13.123 --> 11:14.917
I've got somewhere to be for a minute.

11:14.917 --> 11:17.619
Where are you going all of a sudden?

11:18.754 --> 11:19.866
Something came up.

11:19.866 --> 11:23.383
Come on, the operation's right around
the corner. What could be so urgent?

11:23.383 --> 11:24.801
You think I don't have things to do?

11:24.801 --> 11:26.803
I've got plenty to check
before closing up too.

11:26.803 --> 11:30.548
And we've still got details to review.
Where do you think you're going?

11:34.645 --> 11:36.104
Alright, alright.

11:36.104 --> 11:38.190
Don't worry about it, just go.

11:38.190 --> 11:40.400
Just go. I'll handle things here.

11:40.400 --> 11:42.310
What's with you now, Mr. Cho?

11:44.905 --> 11:47.699
- What about the operation briefing?
- I'll handle it, let's go.

11:47.699 --> 11:50.661
- I was thinking we needed a strategy...
- We can handle it ourselves without him.

11:50.661 --> 11:52.746
We've done plenty without him before.
We can manage by ourselves. Let's go.

11:52.746 --> 11:55.448
That's because without him,
it's less effective.

12:03.840 --> 12:07.330
You know where Jeong Ho Myung went,
right, Mr. Cho?

12:07.330 --> 12:10.097
I told you, he went to
take care of something.

12:10.097 --> 12:14.184
A few hours before the operation
and suddenly he remembers an errand?

12:14.184 --> 12:16.979
Be honest with us.
Something happened, didn't it?

12:16.979 --> 12:18.855
That's not it.

12:18.855 --> 12:22.401
Earlier, you brought up family, Gong Bok.
I think it got to him.

12:22.401 --> 12:25.737
Family talk? What family talk?

12:25.737 --> 12:28.731
Are you talking about
my undercover marriage joke from earlier?

12:29.366 --> 12:32.494
- So it really was an undercover marriage?
- Don't be ridiculous.

12:32.494 --> 12:34.162
No, that's not it.

12:34.162 --> 12:36.648
It's his first operation
since starting a family.

12:36.648 --> 12:38.709
He's probably got a lot on his mind.

12:38.709 --> 12:42.921
Especially since he knows better than anyone
how dangerous Han Kyung Wook is.

12:42.921 --> 12:44.172
What do you mean he knows?

12:44.172 --> 12:46.883
Jeong Ho Myung and Han Kyung Wook

12:46.883 --> 12:49.836
were acquainted
even before the ferry operation?

12:54.488 --> 12:55.542
I shouldn't have said that.

12:55.542 --> 12:57.477
No, please tell us. Okay?

12:57.477 --> 13:00.772
We deserve to know why he's acting like this

13:00.772 --> 13:03.474
right before the operation, right?

13:05.360 --> 13:08.196
Back when Ho Myung was with the NIS,

13:08.196 --> 13:10.991
he worked on the same team as Han Kyung Wook.

13:10.991 --> 13:13.452
Mr. Jeong and Han Kyung Wook
were on the same team?

13:13.452 --> 13:15.153
Yeah.

13:16.288 --> 13:19.416
Before everything happened,

13:19.416 --> 13:21.534
they'd worked together for years.

13:21.534 --> 13:25.564
[12 Years Ago]

13:43.648 --> 13:45.901
I've entered the target area.

13:45.901 --> 13:47.361
You're saying the mole is here, right?

13:47.361 --> 13:50.155
That's right. A lot of agents died

13:50.155 --> 13:52.199
because of the information that mole leaked.

13:52.199 --> 13:55.869
We can't let a traitor like that escape
without paying for his crimes.

13:55.869 --> 13:58.163
Shoot on sight as soon as they appear.

13:58.163 --> 13:59.906
Yes, understood.

14:36.284 --> 14:38.653
You know why I'm here, don't you?

14:56.179 --> 14:58.089
- You...
- Ho Myung.

14:58.765 --> 15:02.185
- Just listen to me.
- Was it you?

15:02.185 --> 15:03.728
The traitor who sold out his own teammates?

15:03.728 --> 15:06.064
No, you know it's not true.

15:06.064 --> 15:10.610
You know how I've been used and discarded
for this country.

15:10.610 --> 15:13.822
Then why are you here
when you're supposed to be in the North?

15:13.822 --> 15:15.615
Mr. Han confirmed it himself.

15:15.615 --> 15:21.621
The guy who came here today to
trade operative information is the traitor.

15:21.621 --> 15:27.127
Ho Myung, you're being deceived
by Mr. Han now.

15:27.127 --> 15:31.840
Mr. Han is the one
who framed me and forced me

15:31.840 --> 15:34.843
- into hiding.
- Don't talk nonsense!

15:34.843 --> 15:36.261
Why would he do that?

15:36.261 --> 15:39.630
Mr. Han is up to something.

15:40.307 --> 15:42.508
He thinks I'm onto him,

15:44.686 --> 15:47.230
so he's trying to eliminate me.

15:47.230 --> 15:49.649
What exactly is he up to?

15:49.649 --> 15:51.067
Can you prove it?

15:51.067 --> 15:52.768
Well, that's...

15:57.824 --> 16:01.703
Ho Myung, just ten minutes.

16:01.703 --> 16:04.030
- What?
- In just 10 minutes,

16:06.208 --> 16:07.876
my daughter will be here.

16:07.876 --> 16:11.254
I haven't seen her in six years
since she was a baby.

16:11.254 --> 16:15.499
Just let me have one meal with my daughter.

16:18.595 --> 16:19.679
Don't lie.

16:19.679 --> 16:21.848
I'm not lying.

16:21.848 --> 16:24.100
It's just ten minutes.

16:24.100 --> 16:26.144
When my daughter comes in ten minutes,

16:26.144 --> 16:28.605
I'll just have dinner with her,

16:28.605 --> 16:30.306
and then I'll go with you.

16:31.107 --> 16:34.110
After that, do whatever you want with me.

16:34.110 --> 16:39.065
Ho Myung, if I can just tell you
about Mr. Han...

16:45.956 --> 16:47.657
Sir.

17:08.979 --> 17:12.974
Weren't you ordered
to eliminate him on sight?

17:13.608 --> 17:17.436
I came just in case,
and it's a good thing I did.

17:18.613 --> 17:21.866
Jeong Ho Myung,
you're supposed to be an agent.

17:21.866 --> 17:23.410
How could you fall
for that kind of sweet talk?

17:23.410 --> 17:26.496
He was once one of your team members, sir.

17:26.496 --> 17:31.084
Couldn't you at least hear him out?

17:31.084 --> 17:32.785
Hear him out?

17:34.337 --> 17:38.008
He said he wasn't here for the deal.

17:38.008 --> 17:39.959
He said his daughter was coming,

17:40.635 --> 17:43.004
and he'd come with us
after having dinner with her.

17:45.015 --> 17:47.216
You believed a lie like that?

17:48.184 --> 17:50.428
Where's his daughter, then?

17:54.065 --> 17:56.610
You should know that cheap emotions

17:56.610 --> 17:59.478
are nothing but weaknesses for an agent.

18:03.033 --> 18:05.818
I wasted time on something pointless.

18:07.329 --> 18:09.447
Just clean up the mess and get back.

19:08.473 --> 19:10.725
That incident hit him hard,

19:10.725 --> 19:13.803
and he repeatedly asked to leave the field.

19:14.521 --> 19:16.555
All were rejected, though.

19:18.024 --> 19:22.195
If Han Kyung Wook finds out
that Ho Myung is married and has a son,

19:22.195 --> 19:24.364
there's no telling what he might do.

19:24.364 --> 19:28.609
[Chinese Traditional Dumplings]
He never shows it, but I'm sure he's worried.

19:39.629 --> 19:41.131
You want me to pull out?

19:41.131 --> 19:43.049
[7 Years Ago]
At O Ran Chinese Restaurant?

19:43.049 --> 19:44.759
That's right.

19:44.759 --> 19:47.721
You haven't gotten any closer
to Bulgae while staying here.

19:47.721 --> 19:49.672
But still...

19:51.224 --> 19:52.976
Do I really need to move?

19:52.976 --> 19:56.312
It's dangerous to stay in one place too long.
Your cover could be blown.

19:56.312 --> 19:58.222
You know exactly why.
Why are you acting like that?

19:59.023 --> 20:02.810
It's time to move.
Start getting your affairs in order.

20:04.571 --> 20:06.272
Yeah...

20:08.742 --> 20:10.470
In order...

20:13.530 --> 20:15.832
Jjambbong.

20:15.832 --> 20:17.992
Thank you.

20:47.322 --> 20:48.782
Um, Ho Myung.

20:48.782 --> 20:49.949
Yeah?

20:49.949 --> 20:52.452
After we close the store,

20:52.452 --> 20:54.370
there's something I want to talk about.

20:54.370 --> 20:55.497
Talk about?

20:55.497 --> 20:57.198
Yeah.

21:02.420 --> 21:05.632
No, I don't want a drink.

21:05.632 --> 21:09.418
- Why not?
- Well, it's just...

21:14.474 --> 21:19.687
Ho Myung, remember how I said
I hadn't been feeling well lately?

21:19.687 --> 21:21.722
You're still not feeling well?

21:23.358 --> 21:26.894
Well, I'm pregnant.

21:33.952 --> 21:35.653
Pre...

21:37.038 --> 21:38.739
Pregnant?

21:39.958 --> 21:42.752
I confirmed it at the hospital yesterday.

21:42.752 --> 21:44.620
I'm eight weeks along.

21:48.925 --> 21:53.012
I'm not telling you to pressure you,
Ho Myung. I'll handle it myself.

21:53.012 --> 21:55.005
What do you mean you'll handle it yourself?

21:56.850 --> 22:00.228
Honestly, with you, Ho Myung,

22:00.228 --> 22:05.307
what we had was just
a brief fling, wasn't it?

22:06.860 --> 22:08.686
What are you talking about?

22:10.530 --> 22:12.991
You and I, Ho Myung,

22:12.991 --> 22:15.609
we've been together a long time,

22:16.494 --> 22:18.696
and I barely know anything

22:19.330 --> 22:21.708
about you, Ho Myung, right?

22:21.708 --> 22:27.088
I don't know what kind of person you were
before or why you came to Yeongseondo Island.

22:27.088 --> 22:32.251
I've never even heard stories
about your family or friends.

22:32.927 --> 22:37.640
But Ho Myung,
you don't really plan on explaining

22:37.640 --> 22:43.178
all your personal circumstances
to me from now on, do you?

22:51.988 --> 22:58.620
I'm almost forty, and honestly,
having a child is a bit scary.

22:58.620 --> 23:01.539
And I don't even know

23:01.539 --> 23:05.242
if I can raise a child properly,
and the restaurant keeps me busy too.

23:05.960 --> 23:09.839
Anyway, that's all I had to say,
so enjoy your drink.

23:09.839 --> 23:12.008
I don't want to drink.

23:12.008 --> 23:13.709
Huh?

23:16.679 --> 23:18.714
I won't drink by myself.

23:19.682 --> 23:21.925
Let's have a drink together
after the baby's born.

23:24.938 --> 23:29.808
What... what are you talking about?

23:31.027 --> 23:33.279
Let's keep this baby.

23:33.279 --> 23:36.824
No, it's not exactly something
you can talk about so easily, is it?

23:36.824 --> 23:38.859
I'm not saying it lightly.

23:40.286 --> 23:45.866
Actually, my parents died when I was young,

23:47.043 --> 23:50.046
so I grew up not really knowing
what family meant.

23:50.046 --> 23:53.415
I never imagined marriage, children,

23:54.258 --> 23:57.211
a family, or anything like that.

23:58.137 --> 24:01.307
But when I heard we're having a child,

24:01.307 --> 24:05.886
I can't... I can't even explain
what I'm feeling.

24:06.854 --> 24:08.722
But this thought came to me.

24:10.483 --> 24:12.151
No matter what happens,

24:12.151 --> 24:13.936
I want to be by your side

24:14.612 --> 24:16.814
and our baby's side.

24:19.242 --> 24:22.486
Let's get married, O Ran.

24:46.185 --> 24:47.979
Ho Myung, what are you doing here?

24:47.979 --> 24:49.022
Why aren't you coming inside?

24:49.022 --> 24:51.065
You startled me.

24:51.065 --> 24:53.892
Didn't you come to make up with O Ran?

24:58.948 --> 25:01.868
Did you write the letter?
You wrote it, right?

25:01.868 --> 25:04.078
- No.
- What? Why?

25:04.078 --> 25:08.416
Well... I just didn't know what to write.

25:08.416 --> 25:10.793
You still don't know O Ran?

25:10.793 --> 25:15.048
A few sweet words,
and she'll soften right up.

25:15.048 --> 25:17.875
She got her good nature from me.

25:18.926 --> 25:23.681
I don't think a few words
will fix things this time.

25:23.681 --> 25:25.725
I wasn't exactly in the right.

25:25.725 --> 25:29.303
I think it'd only make her angrier.

25:33.149 --> 25:37.519
Do you know why I came to Yeongseondo Island?

25:38.362 --> 25:39.989
I heard it was your hometown.

25:39.989 --> 25:43.367
No, I got scammed
out of all the money I'd saved

25:43.367 --> 25:46.579
to open a restaurant in Seoul,
so I ended up here.

25:46.579 --> 25:48.498
What?

25:48.498 --> 25:53.044
I couldn't tell your mother-in-law
because of my pride.

25:53.044 --> 25:55.213
I lied and said I wanted to settle here

25:55.213 --> 25:59.166
because it was my hometown.

26:00.218 --> 26:03.805
She probably knew the truth.

26:03.805 --> 26:05.890
But she never said a word.

26:05.890 --> 26:09.477
She followed me here without
a single complaint, even while pregnant.

26:09.477 --> 26:12.313
Knowing the truth would've only hurt her.

26:12.313 --> 26:13.815
So I kept quiet.

26:13.815 --> 26:18.277
I thought I'd tell her
once the business succeeded.

26:18.277 --> 26:23.106
Then again... I never got to tell her.

26:26.661 --> 26:30.289
I should've just told her.

26:30.289 --> 26:35.044
Why I worked without a day off,

26:35.044 --> 26:38.539
why I kept working even when I was sick.

26:42.009 --> 26:47.381
Then, when she left,
she might've felt less disappointed in me.

26:51.978 --> 26:56.065
Don't live with regrets like I did.
Be honest with her.

26:56.065 --> 26:59.861
What can't a married couple work through?

26:59.861 --> 27:04.690
So don't leave O Ran feeling that hurt.

27:07.160 --> 27:09.412
Yes, I understand.

27:09.412 --> 27:10.454
Yeah?

27:10.454 --> 27:14.584
- Then now...
- Right now, I have some things to sort out.

27:14.584 --> 27:20.047
Next time I come, I'll tell her
everything I couldn't bring myself

27:20.047 --> 27:24.543
to tell her, just like you said.

27:25.511 --> 27:27.546
Goodness.

27:28.514 --> 27:30.308
You know?

27:30.308 --> 27:33.269
Apologies are all about timing.

27:33.269 --> 27:36.847
Yes, it won't be that late.

27:48.409 --> 27:51.787
It's been a while
since I've taken the stage myself.

27:51.787 --> 27:53.614
I'm oddly nervous.

27:54.832 --> 27:57.460
Shall we do a final check on the progress?

27:57.460 --> 28:00.245
We've definitely dried up
Ja Ae-won Orphanage's funding source, right?

28:00.245 --> 28:01.505
[Replenish vigor]

28:01.505 --> 28:03.749
Why bother with this again?

28:10.348 --> 28:12.683
Thanks to Mr. Han's foresight,

28:12.683 --> 28:14.810
things went smoothly.

28:14.810 --> 28:16.896
- Sir!
- The Ja Ae-won Orphanage building is old,

28:16.896 --> 28:18.940
- Sir!
- so we make an issue of aging facilities.

28:18.940 --> 28:22.026
But it's not even inspection day yet.

28:22.026 --> 28:24.654
Ma'am, if we come on a scheduled date,

28:24.654 --> 28:27.648
it's not a surprise inspection, right?

28:28.282 --> 28:30.534
The financial situation
of Ja Ae-won Orphanage is obvious.

28:30.534 --> 28:32.411
It's true the facilities are outdated.

28:32.411 --> 28:36.666
Even so, where are our children
supposed to go if you do this?

28:36.666 --> 28:39.835
In any case, we've issued a warning
according to regulations.

28:39.835 --> 28:43.631
Either spend personal funds on repairs,
or close the facility.

28:43.631 --> 28:45.174
Fix the problem immediately.

28:45.174 --> 28:47.134
Since it's hard to arrange repair funds,

28:47.134 --> 28:50.012
they'll have no choice
but to do exactly what we want.

28:50.012 --> 28:52.848
- What about the donors?
- There weren't any major donors.

28:52.848 --> 28:56.811
Other than government subsidies,
it's mostly small donations from individuals.

28:56.811 --> 29:00.940
And most of those come out
of Kim Seon Jung and his wife's own pockets.

29:00.940 --> 29:04.777
See? Being too clean can be a problem.

29:04.777 --> 29:06.612
Okay, good job.

29:06.612 --> 29:12.985
Now then, let's help ourselves to the feast
that's already been prepared.

29:17.164 --> 29:18.541
- Chairman, you're here.
- Oh, dear.

29:18.541 --> 29:19.667
Why did you come out here?

29:19.667 --> 29:20.876
Yes.

29:20.876 --> 29:22.837
- You've been well, right?
- Of course.

29:22.837 --> 29:24.255
What do you mean the loan was denied?

29:24.255 --> 29:27.008
I'm sorry, but we made our decision

29:27.008 --> 29:29.719
after evaluating your credit
and collateral value.

29:29.719 --> 29:33.306
Your loan application was deemed ineligible
during the approval process.

29:33.306 --> 29:36.267
But last time, the branch manager said
it would be approved.

29:36.267 --> 29:39.302
Please check one more time, okay?

29:42.940 --> 29:44.650
Sir!

29:44.650 --> 29:46.351
Well...

29:48.988 --> 29:51.115
Ma'am, what brings you here?

29:51.115 --> 29:53.701
Ma'am, please don't do this here.

29:53.701 --> 29:55.119
Let's talk privately.

29:55.119 --> 29:58.789
Well, why is the loan suddenly being denied?

29:58.789 --> 30:01.751
If this falls through
and the orphanage closes,

30:01.751 --> 30:04.170
what should we do with the children?

30:04.170 --> 30:07.089
Excuse me, what do you mean, children?

30:07.089 --> 30:10.009
She's running an orphanage,

30:10.009 --> 30:12.794
and there seems to be a misunderstanding.

30:13.721 --> 30:17.558
If you don't mind,
could I hear her out as well?

30:17.558 --> 30:20.968
I'm having trouble understanding this.

30:20.968 --> 30:26.317
This lady seems to be someone
who devotes herself to society.

30:26.317 --> 30:29.737
So why was her loan suddenly blocked?

30:29.737 --> 30:33.157
Well, it's that there are

30:33.157 --> 30:36.369
various policy considerations
when it comes to loans.

30:36.369 --> 30:41.374
But those policies don't just
change overnight, do they?

30:41.374 --> 30:43.084
- What do you think?
- Exactly.

30:43.084 --> 30:45.378
You said there was no problem before.

30:45.378 --> 30:48.756
So did you actually review this properly?

30:48.756 --> 30:49.840
Well, it's just...

30:49.840 --> 30:53.886
If this bank can suddenly
deny loans overnight,

30:53.886 --> 30:56.555
my trust in this bank drops dramatically.

30:56.555 --> 31:00.142
Who knows? Maybe you might be the one

31:00.142 --> 31:02.937
changing your story at the drop of a hat.

31:02.937 --> 31:04.721
No, Chairman...

31:04.721 --> 31:08.609
Ms. Kim, bring me the paperwork
for this lady's loan.

31:08.609 --> 31:10.778
I'll review it myself.

31:10.778 --> 31:12.154
Yes, understood.

31:12.154 --> 31:14.064
Good. Hurry up.

31:15.700 --> 31:17.484
Chairman!

31:18.744 --> 31:20.996
I didn't get a chance to thank you earlier.

31:20.996 --> 31:22.536
Thank you for your help.

31:22.536 --> 31:25.376
Not at all. Did the issue get resolved well?

31:25.376 --> 31:30.005
Yes, thanks to you,
I think the loan will be approved.

31:30.005 --> 31:31.560
I don't know how to thank you.

31:31.560 --> 31:34.176
Oh, never mind, never mind.

31:34.176 --> 31:36.345
Seeing how worried you were

31:36.345 --> 31:39.348
about the children ending up on the streets

31:39.348 --> 31:41.591
reminded me of my past.

31:42.601 --> 31:45.229
When I was young,
my father's business failed,

31:45.229 --> 31:47.273
and I ended up
wandering the streets of the Philippines.

31:47.273 --> 31:49.024
Oh my, really?

31:49.024 --> 31:53.320
Back then, I made a promise to myself.

31:53.320 --> 31:57.450
That I'd never turn my back
on people in need. But...

31:57.450 --> 32:00.119
I used being busy as an excuse
and forgot all about it.

32:00.119 --> 32:01.454
I don't think you forgot at all.

32:01.454 --> 32:04.540
You helped our children tremendously today.

32:04.540 --> 32:05.749
Not at all.

32:05.749 --> 32:11.422
I've actually realized so much
by meeting you today, ma'am.

32:11.422 --> 32:13.966
It made me wonder if I've spent too much time

32:13.966 --> 32:17.636
looking ahead
and not enough time looking around.

32:17.636 --> 32:20.297
To be honest, I feel a little ashamed.

32:21.682 --> 32:23.726
So, if you don't mind,

32:23.726 --> 32:28.104
I'd like to give the children
at the orphanage a little gift.

32:28.104 --> 32:29.356
Would that be okay?

32:29.356 --> 32:30.649
Pardon?

32:30.649 --> 32:31.892
A gift.

32:33.194 --> 32:35.560
Yes, as long as it's handled
through the proper procedures.

32:35.560 --> 32:40.075
Oh, it's nothing big enough to require that.

32:40.075 --> 32:43.695
Just something that needs your approval.

32:44.747 --> 32:47.875
We try to operate transparently,

32:47.875 --> 32:52.046
so we don't accept
private donations or gifts.

32:52.046 --> 32:54.882
I'm sorry, but we appreciate the thought.

32:54.882 --> 32:59.261
No, no, no, it's not something grand or big.

32:59.261 --> 33:01.639
So I actually feel embarrassed.

33:01.639 --> 33:05.267
The old books from our hotel lounge,
did you discard them all?

33:05.267 --> 33:06.685
We still have them.

33:06.685 --> 33:07.937
Alright.

33:07.937 --> 33:09.897
It's not much,

33:09.897 --> 33:11.784
but how about I donate these books
to the children?

33:11.784 --> 33:15.110
This idea just popped into my mind.

33:15.110 --> 33:16.487
- Books?
- Yes.

33:16.487 --> 33:17.530
The books.

33:17.530 --> 33:19.990
Not money or material things,

33:19.990 --> 33:22.368
just food for the soul, you know?

33:22.368 --> 33:24.328
They're only a few used books.

33:24.328 --> 33:27.364
Would that still be too much?

33:30.184 --> 33:32.040
[Jeongseok Study Residence]

33:57.695 --> 34:01.314
It was only for a moment,
but his moves were definitely unusual.

34:04.618 --> 34:07.162
And the amnesia too.

34:07.162 --> 34:10.407
The more I think about it,
the more suspicious he seems.

34:15.629 --> 34:20.175
Look over there. Prosecutor Kang has been
staring at Bong Jae Soon the whole time.

34:20.175 --> 34:24.638
Those two definitely have something going on.

34:24.638 --> 34:27.558
Not something romantic,
it looks like they just want to argue.

34:27.558 --> 34:31.261
Ye Ji, what would you know? Lifelong single.

34:38.944 --> 34:42.647
Mr. Bong, something happened
between the two of you, right?

34:44.366 --> 34:46.160
Nothing happened.

34:46.160 --> 34:49.246
Back in the day,
I had quite a way with women.

34:49.246 --> 34:51.665
When a woman looks at you like that,

34:51.665 --> 34:55.785
it's either because she lost money to you
or has an interest.

34:59.089 --> 35:01.082
This is so good.

35:03.427 --> 35:06.680
Come on, be honest.
Mr. Bong, you have some feelings too, right?

35:06.680 --> 35:10.508
It's not like that. We've just...

35:11.644 --> 35:13.896
We've gotten a bit closer, that's all.

35:13.896 --> 35:18.725
Well, I should go bring some soup over there.

35:25.074 --> 35:27.275
So busy.

35:28.535 --> 35:30.663
This is so good.

35:30.663 --> 35:32.739
I'm on duty tomorrow.

35:37.832 --> 35:39.464
Darn it.

35:44.510 --> 35:46.294
Please eat.

35:49.515 --> 35:52.351
Excuse me, sir. Could you please uncuff me?

35:52.351 --> 35:54.561
I'm not a criminal. What's with this?

35:54.561 --> 35:56.304
Please eat.

35:58.524 --> 36:01.643
How am I supposed to eat
with my hands like this?

36:07.366 --> 36:09.660
Please eat. Open your mouth.

36:12.454 --> 36:13.747
Jeez.

36:13.747 --> 36:15.541
Do you realize this is a serious crime?

36:15.541 --> 36:21.046
The serious crime is what you did
with those Heaven Capital guys.

36:21.046 --> 36:23.998
If you don't want to eat, don't.
Don't waste the rice.

36:24.633 --> 36:26.760
Wait! Hold on, hold on!

36:26.760 --> 36:30.264
Aren't you that martial arts master
the Heaven Capital guys were after?

36:30.264 --> 36:32.182
The one who fought seventeen alone?
Or was it eighteen?

36:32.182 --> 36:34.017
And those moves you pulled yesterday.

36:34.017 --> 36:35.644
It's definitely you!

36:35.644 --> 36:37.980
Master, it's an honor to meet you.

36:37.980 --> 36:39.310
Could you uncuff me?

36:39.310 --> 36:41.650
If you do, I'll talk to them for you,

36:41.650 --> 36:43.777
and tell them not to bother you again.

36:43.777 --> 36:46.563
I can do that for you, okay?

36:50.536 --> 36:52.777
Please eat.

36:59.585 --> 37:01.453
Oh, my!

37:11.656 --> 37:13.097
Oh, my.

37:13.807 --> 37:15.758
What are you doing?

37:17.895 --> 37:21.014
I got dizzy and just leaned
against the door for a second.

37:25.360 --> 37:27.187
Oh, no.

37:38.582 --> 37:40.408
Please eat.

37:45.416 --> 37:50.312
Alright, there we are.

37:55.432 --> 37:57.100
You look much happier.

37:57.100 --> 38:00.437
Feeling relieved
now that the loan's coming through?

38:00.437 --> 38:03.398
Of course, I was so anxious about it.

38:03.398 --> 38:05.984
You know, the person I met at the bank

38:05.984 --> 38:09.238
said they would donate to the orphanage.

38:09.238 --> 38:11.198
Donate? Who?

38:11.198 --> 38:13.867
Chairman Do Hyeon Tae of Heaven Hotel.

38:13.867 --> 38:15.327
He said they have a lot of old books

38:15.327 --> 38:18.696
they'd otherwise throw away,
so he wants to give them to the children.

38:19.998 --> 38:24.577
Do Hyeon Tae...
The chairman of Heaven Casino?

38:25.796 --> 38:29.174
Someone who's never shown
the slightest interest in philanthropy

38:29.174 --> 38:31.584
suddenly wants to donate?

38:33.512 --> 38:35.296
That's weird.

38:37.599 --> 38:41.645
Well, turn that down.

38:41.645 --> 38:46.108
Wait, it's just a book donation, not money.

38:46.108 --> 38:50.404
You never know what kind of agenda
a businessman like that has.

38:50.404 --> 38:53.073
Either way, don't accept anything.
I clearly told you.

38:53.073 --> 38:55.617
You've become quite the politician.

38:55.617 --> 38:59.746
He was doing this out of pure goodwill.
Can't you see it that way?

38:59.746 --> 39:02.082
That's not it. I'm just saying
we should be careful.

39:02.082 --> 39:04.084
It's only a few old books.

39:04.084 --> 39:05.448
There are more important things
to worry about.

39:05.448 --> 39:09.205
Should the kids miss out on books
just because you're being cautious?

39:17.224 --> 39:20.100
Alright, maybe I overreacted.

39:20.100 --> 39:23.604
It's only a few old books.
Go ahead and take them.

39:23.604 --> 39:26.598
- Really?
- Yeah.

39:34.281 --> 39:35.824
Chairman,

39:35.824 --> 39:38.619
[Donated items]
we received the old books.

39:38.619 --> 39:41.997
Thank you for the meaningful donation.

39:41.997 --> 39:43.707
Your generosity will be

39:43.707 --> 39:48.036
a great source of inspiration
for the children.

39:52.007 --> 39:54.834
The bomb has been delivered.

39:56.762 --> 40:00.849
I handpicked only the pieces
from my favorite collection.

40:00.849 --> 40:04.561
You didn't just deliver them
and leave, did you?

40:04.561 --> 40:06.063
Of course not.

40:06.063 --> 40:09.515
I've already arranged with the staff
inside the orphanage.

40:10.442 --> 40:13.640
I made it very clear
that if they don't want their life ruined

40:13.640 --> 40:16.240
by gambling debts,
they'd better sell the paintings.

40:16.240 --> 40:19.576
The proceeds will be quietly donated
to Ja Ae-won Orphanage

40:19.576 --> 40:22.287
without Kim Seon Jung's wife ever knowing.

40:22.287 --> 40:24.831
The moment you press this button,

40:24.831 --> 40:27.668
Kim Seon Jung will no longer be

40:27.668 --> 40:29.836
Imcheon's clean mayoral candidate.

40:29.836 --> 40:33.799
He'll become a corrupt politician
who used Ja Ae-won Orphanage

40:33.799 --> 40:36.959
to funnel illegal campaign funds.

40:39.680 --> 40:42.224
- That's neat.
- Thank you.

40:42.224 --> 40:45.060
So, should we blow it open right away?

40:45.060 --> 40:47.437
Since we're going to blow it up,

40:47.437 --> 40:49.898
it's only fun if there's a bit of a show.

40:49.898 --> 40:51.024
What kind of show?

40:51.024 --> 40:53.610
- Chief Baek.
- Yes.

40:53.610 --> 40:56.905
Let's go grab a bowl
of rice soup sometime soon.

40:56.905 --> 40:58.606
Alright.

41:04.413 --> 41:06.123
What are you talking about?

41:06.123 --> 41:07.791
I was planning to go.

41:07.791 --> 41:10.836
But the broker we've been tracking
for three months just resurfaced.

41:10.836 --> 41:14.080
This is a huge case.

41:14.756 --> 41:16.758
Alright, alright.

41:16.758 --> 41:19.011
If you can't come, then send someone else.

41:19.011 --> 41:21.304
This broker is a big fish too.

41:21.304 --> 41:24.599
And Chief gave special orders, so everyone
from the station is already mobilized.

41:24.599 --> 41:26.440
- Sir.
- I'll go right away, hold on.

41:26.440 --> 41:28.979
Ma'am, at least try to gather some evidence.

41:28.979 --> 41:30.689
I'll join you
as soon as I wrap things up here.

41:30.689 --> 41:33.900
What kind of evidence do we need
when we can just raid the scene?

41:33.900 --> 41:35.601
Hello?

41:39.781 --> 41:41.992
I thought these guys were
only taking people's money.

41:41.992 --> 41:44.411
But they're bringing in drugs too.

41:44.411 --> 41:46.079
They're complete scum.

41:46.079 --> 41:50.333
But, if Prosecutor Kang
ties these corrupt cops

41:50.333 --> 41:52.461
and the Heaven Capital guys to the drug case,

41:52.461 --> 41:55.422
can we really bring them all down?

41:55.422 --> 41:57.340
I think so.

41:57.340 --> 41:59.426
Then the Yeongseon precinct
will finally be cleaned up.

41:59.426 --> 42:02.137
And once they're behind bars,
everything they've done

42:02.137 --> 42:04.514
will be revealed one by one.

42:04.514 --> 42:07.851
Hopefully, we might even get my house back.

42:07.851 --> 42:09.519
I'm sorry.

42:09.519 --> 42:13.523
I don't think the detectives
will be joining us at the bust today.

42:13.523 --> 42:14.649
- Why not?
- What?

42:14.649 --> 42:15.776
Why?

42:15.776 --> 42:18.195
So we're just supposed to sit here and watch?

42:18.195 --> 42:20.405
No, I'm going by myself if I have to.

42:20.405 --> 42:23.325
We need evidence if we're going
to have any chance moving forward.

42:23.325 --> 42:26.286
- You're going alone, Prosecutor?
- Do you want to go together, Jae Soon?

42:26.286 --> 42:28.955
Mi Kyeong, would you come along with me?

42:28.955 --> 42:30.749
- Yes.
- Come on!

42:30.749 --> 42:32.834
I have to go too. I'm not just a civilian.

42:32.834 --> 42:35.587
- I can definitely help.
- I'll come along.

42:35.587 --> 42:37.756
We need to catch these guys
if I'm ever going to get my home back.

42:37.756 --> 42:39.299
I'll do whatever I can.

42:39.299 --> 42:40.550
- Let me come with you.
- Hold on.

42:40.550 --> 42:44.221
That's no ordinary dangerous operation.

42:44.221 --> 42:46.389
Then all the more reason
we should go together.

42:46.389 --> 42:49.175
How can you think about going alone
when it's that dangerous?

42:50.560 --> 42:52.261
- Right?
- Yes.

42:56.900 --> 42:59.236
- You're here, boss!
- You're here, boss!

42:59.236 --> 43:00.695
Is this everyone?

43:00.695 --> 43:02.396
Yes.

43:03.532 --> 43:05.200
As I mentioned before,

43:05.200 --> 43:08.120
to move without attracting the eyes
of Mr. Han and Chairman Do,

43:08.120 --> 43:09.454
this is the most we can gather.

43:09.454 --> 43:13.041
Neither Mr. Han nor Chairman Do
is of any use to me anymore.

43:13.041 --> 43:14.501
Don't worry too much, boss.

43:14.501 --> 43:17.712
We've got about thirty rookies
waiting near the harbor.

43:17.712 --> 43:22.050
No martial arts master
can handle that many people alone.

43:22.050 --> 43:24.636
We'll just have to work with what we've got.

43:24.636 --> 43:27.931
Today is a very historic day
for our In Goo faction.

43:27.931 --> 43:31.184
Anyone who screws up answers to me.

43:31.184 --> 43:34.595
- Don't let your guard down!
- Yes, sir!

43:40.986 --> 43:43.071
- Hey, you're here too?
- Yeah, Jin Soo.

43:43.071 --> 43:46.399
- Nam Il, you are here too.
- I heard the pay is good.

43:49.578 --> 43:51.830
Why'd you bring Nam Il along?
He wasn't even needed.

43:51.830 --> 43:54.124
He said he's desperate for money.

43:54.124 --> 43:56.001
Cut him some slack.

43:56.001 --> 43:59.453
By the way, what are we doing here?

44:00.130 --> 44:02.915
- Why do we need weapons?
- Not sure.

44:37.709 --> 44:39.586
You're here, boss.

44:39.586 --> 44:41.463
This kid's got spirit.

44:41.463 --> 44:43.840
- Hey, at ease.
- Yes, sir.

44:43.840 --> 44:46.134
- Is everyone here?
- Yes, we've gathered everyone, boss.

44:46.134 --> 44:48.669
- Okay, get into position.
- To positions!

44:52.182 --> 44:57.145
Listen up, a very important shipment
for the In Goo faction is arriving today.

44:57.145 --> 44:59.564
All you have to do is stand guard

44:59.564 --> 45:01.775
and make sure that punk

45:01.775 --> 45:04.185
doesn't get his hands on it.

45:04.861 --> 45:07.155
Anyone who does well today

45:07.155 --> 45:11.493
will be hired as our permanent employee
with full benefits, got it?

45:11.493 --> 45:13.611
- Yes, understood!
- Yes, understood!

45:16.164 --> 45:18.658
What's with this guy? Hey, come out.

45:20.418 --> 45:22.671
Huh?

45:22.671 --> 45:24.631
What?

45:24.631 --> 45:26.508
Hey, you, come over here.

45:26.508 --> 45:28.176
- Why?
- Just come over here.

45:28.176 --> 45:31.170
Hey, catch that guy! Get him! Get him!

45:34.472 --> 45:36.921
- Come here.
- Darn it!

45:37.686 --> 45:39.387
Boss.

45:41.356 --> 45:43.233
Isn't this that martial arts master's nephew?

45:43.233 --> 45:44.609
Huh?

45:44.609 --> 45:46.027
- No, I'm not.
- It's him, boss.

45:46.027 --> 45:47.404
You've got the wrong guy.

45:47.404 --> 45:49.406
What's with the denial?

45:49.406 --> 45:51.741
What did I tell you? Wasn't I right?

45:51.741 --> 45:54.360
I said that martial arts master
would show up.

45:55.078 --> 45:58.873
Even planted his nephew as a spy.
He really came prepared.

45:58.873 --> 46:02.043
- What should we do, boss?
- What do you mean what do we do?

46:02.043 --> 46:06.247
Just be grateful and take the opportunity
we've been given.

46:08.049 --> 46:11.460
You punk, huh?

46:30.613 --> 46:31.906
Wow!

46:31.906 --> 46:35.452
It's been a while
since I've smelled action like this.

46:35.452 --> 46:37.245
So what should we do now?

46:37.245 --> 46:40.957
Should we go crack down
on the Heaven Capital guys?

46:40.957 --> 46:45.253
I think it'd be better
if I move alone from here.

46:45.253 --> 46:46.546
What are you planning to do by yourself?

46:46.546 --> 46:49.257
Why? I was looking forward
to getting some action myself.

46:49.257 --> 46:53.678
If we move as a group in a place this open,
we'll stand out immediately.

46:53.678 --> 46:55.847
I'll go in alone, secure the evidence,
and come right back.

46:55.847 --> 46:59.759
- Everyone, please wait in the car.
- Then hold on a second.

47:00.685 --> 47:02.470
Oh, jeez.

47:04.564 --> 47:08.860
If anything happens,

47:08.860 --> 47:10.487
radio me immediately.

47:10.487 --> 47:12.405
- We'll be there in a flash.
- Thank you.

47:12.405 --> 47:14.106
I'll be back.

47:18.953 --> 47:20.747
She does stand out quite a bit.

47:20.747 --> 47:22.448
A lot.

47:28.880 --> 47:31.257
I think I should follow her.

47:31.257 --> 47:33.218
The prosecutor told us not to follow.

47:33.218 --> 47:39.215
Prosecutor Kang still isn't fully recovered.
Someone should go with her.

47:40.296 --> 47:43.853
Well, I'll be right back.
Just stay here for a moment.

47:43.853 --> 47:45.563
Prosecutor Kang!

47:45.563 --> 47:49.433
I'm telling you, there's something
between those two.

47:59.577 --> 48:01.413
Are you okay?

48:01.413 --> 48:03.114
Yeah.

48:11.589 --> 48:15.260
- The quantity and quality check out, right?
- You think I'd rip you off?

48:15.260 --> 48:17.002
Check for yourself.

48:36.281 --> 48:39.576
But why'd you bring so many people?

48:39.576 --> 48:41.369
Did something go wrong?

48:41.369 --> 48:42.787
What could go wrong?

48:42.787 --> 48:44.664
They're just here for peace of mind.

48:44.664 --> 48:48.168
Well, you've checked the goods.

48:48.168 --> 48:50.170
And you've got your peace of mind.

48:50.170 --> 48:52.788
Now, please sign the receipt.

48:58.219 --> 48:59.345
Good work.

48:59.345 --> 49:01.973
Glad the delivery went smoothly
since we're both getting paid.

49:01.973 --> 49:05.342
I'll let the Chinese guys
know the deal went through.

49:06.186 --> 49:09.013
Good, I've been waiting for this day.

49:09.898 --> 49:11.608
Look at this beautiful little money-maker.

49:11.608 --> 49:13.735
Pack it up quickly, and let's head back.

49:13.735 --> 49:15.195
Don't dawdle, got it?

49:15.195 --> 49:17.146
- Yes, boss.
- Yes, understood.

49:18.740 --> 49:20.983
Yeah, Mr. Kim, lower it.

49:21.618 --> 49:23.569
Yes, understood!

49:33.254 --> 49:36.999
Setup complete. Let's have some fun
for a change, it's been a while.

49:41.471 --> 49:43.172
What the...

49:44.307 --> 49:46.184
Check it out quickly!

49:46.184 --> 49:48.302
Hey, Mr. Kim, I said lower it!

49:50.480 --> 49:52.973
Can't you hear me? Lower it!

49:55.777 --> 50:00.814
Mr. Yoo, what's going on right now?

50:03.117 --> 50:06.445
Everything's going
according to plan. Don't panic.

50:08.164 --> 50:10.699
What are you doing, you punks?
Did you forget Plan B?

50:13.586 --> 50:15.588
Alright, rookies, Plan B.

50:15.588 --> 50:18.174
- Get ready.
- Hey!

50:18.174 --> 50:20.542
- Focus, get ready.
- Yeah.

50:24.552 --> 50:27.383
- Darn it, what's that?
- What's happening?

50:28.601 --> 50:33.514
Oh my, you fools. At your age,
you should be holding pencils, not weapons.

50:35.900 --> 50:38.861
- Stay focused!
- Yeah.

50:38.861 --> 50:41.063
- Go!
- Go! Let's go!

50:42.073 --> 50:43.074
What?

50:43.074 --> 50:44.817
What is it? What's going on?

50:44.817 --> 50:49.831
- Jeez!
- What?

50:49.831 --> 50:50.832
Everybody get ready!

50:50.832 --> 50:51.976
- Yes!
- Yes!

50:51.976 --> 50:54.910
Guys!

50:59.924 --> 51:01.709
Oh, boss!

51:05.221 --> 51:09.350
Martial arts master,
I wondered why you hadn't shown up.

51:09.350 --> 51:12.228
- But there are two of you?
- How many times do I have to tell you?

51:12.228 --> 51:14.105
I told you, it's the Masked Racer!

51:14.105 --> 51:17.942
- Masked Racer!
- Like this!

51:17.942 --> 51:20.361
That crazy masked freak is back?

51:20.361 --> 51:24.198
Whatever it is, why do you keep showing up
and meddling in my business?

51:24.198 --> 51:26.534
Because you keep doing bad things,

51:26.534 --> 51:29.704
Masked Racer keeps showing up.

51:29.704 --> 51:33.082
But I'm not here to interfere today.

51:33.082 --> 51:35.367
I came to watch the first snowfall.

51:36.377 --> 51:38.912
Listen to him talking about the first snow.

51:40.673 --> 51:43.336
You think I'm just gonna nod and let you go

51:43.336 --> 51:46.471
if you start spouting
that kind of sentimental crap?

51:46.471 --> 51:50.558
I've already dug your grave
waiting for you today, you punk.

51:50.558 --> 51:53.311
You shouldn't just try to win with numbers.

51:53.311 --> 51:56.314
You've got to use your head.

51:56.314 --> 52:00.735
Now that we've gathered
all our special guests in one place.

52:00.735 --> 52:05.356
How about we all enjoy
the first snowfall together?

52:31.974 --> 52:34.227
What? What's wrong with this thing?

52:34.227 --> 52:36.553
Press it harder.

52:40.858 --> 52:42.559
It's not working.

52:44.946 --> 52:47.240
Seong Wo, this isn't working.

52:47.240 --> 52:48.328
Maybe it's too old?

52:48.328 --> 52:49.832
Ho Myung.

52:49.832 --> 52:52.537
Press harder, press firmly.

52:52.537 --> 52:54.831
I said press harder, you punk!

52:54.831 --> 52:56.532
Come on!

52:57.417 --> 52:59.419
Ah, it's not working!

52:59.419 --> 53:01.384
- Is this thing broken?
- What are they doing?

53:01.384 --> 53:03.240
Darn it.

53:05.341 --> 53:08.636
- Press harder.
- What are those punks doing?

53:08.636 --> 53:11.255
Check how those bastards even got up there!

53:11.889 --> 53:13.757
Ah, jeez.

53:15.432 --> 53:18.326
Darn it.

53:47.592 --> 53:49.608
- Get them!
- Go get them!

53:55.767 --> 53:57.384
Boss.

53:59.020 --> 54:00.596
No!

54:04.650 --> 54:06.351
You startled me.

56:36.510 --> 56:39.055
Kill every one of them!

56:39.055 --> 56:41.757
- Bring his nephew here.
- What? Nephew?

56:48.582 --> 56:49.800
Jeez!

56:52.068 --> 56:53.319
What are you doing here right now?

56:53.319 --> 56:55.363
Didn't you just hear something like gunshots?

56:55.363 --> 56:58.491
Those guys are so dangerous, Prosecutor Kang.

56:58.491 --> 57:01.276
Just stay put, got it?

57:05.456 --> 57:11.244
- Did you get enough evidence?
- Right now is a very crucial moment.

57:14.507 --> 57:16.634
Wait!

57:16.634 --> 57:19.637
If you don't want to see that kid die,
stop right there!

57:19.637 --> 57:22.181
- It's Nam Il!
- What did you say?

57:22.181 --> 57:24.016
He's my nephew, Nam Il.

57:24.016 --> 57:26.352
Why is he here?

57:26.352 --> 57:28.104
What are you doing? What are you going to do?

57:28.104 --> 57:31.357
I have to save him. He could die there.

57:31.357 --> 57:33.442
Do you have any plan if you go in, Jae Soon?

57:33.442 --> 57:35.194
- Wait, I'll radio for help.
- No, no.

57:35.194 --> 57:37.396
I don't have time for that.

57:40.392 --> 57:43.276
Gosh, why are you doing this?

57:47.123 --> 57:50.918
Prosecutor, please hit my head
hard with this.

57:50.918 --> 57:52.869
You've lost your mind, huh?

57:55.131 --> 57:57.341
I have a plan, trust me.

57:57.341 --> 58:02.221
Believe me, and hit me as hard as you can.

58:02.221 --> 58:04.515
Please.

58:04.515 --> 58:06.851
Please, hurry.

58:06.851 --> 58:08.477
Hurry, hurry.

58:08.477 --> 58:11.263
At this rate, Nam Il is going to die!

58:12.940 --> 58:15.151
Oh my, what should I do?

58:15.151 --> 58:16.810
Jae Soon!

58:17.611 --> 58:19.980
Ugh, I'm going crazy.

58:22.616 --> 58:26.069
Mi Kyeong, please come quickly with the car.
It's an emergency...

58:30.166 --> 58:33.294
If you want to see your nephew die,
go on then!

58:33.294 --> 58:35.671
Nephew? What nephew? You have a nephew?

58:35.671 --> 58:37.873
I've got no nephew, you kidding?

58:42.053 --> 58:46.265
Wait, isn't he... Bulgae's nephew?

58:46.265 --> 58:47.767
Hey, hey, hey, don't do that!

58:47.767 --> 58:50.478
- He has nothing to do with us!
- You think I'll believe that?

58:50.478 --> 58:53.189
I won't be at peace
until I cut this punk's throat.

58:53.189 --> 58:54.356
What the heck?

58:54.356 --> 58:56.224
Grab these guys!

59:43.364 --> 59:45.357
Uncle!

01:00:13.853 --> 01:00:16.388
Hey, you darn punks!

01:00:17.356 --> 01:00:19.316
Come here! Come here!

01:00:19.316 --> 01:00:20.776
I'm Heo Nam Il, okay?

01:00:20.776 --> 01:00:22.862
I'm not dying alone! I'm throwing it!

01:00:22.862 --> 01:00:24.688
I'm really throwing it!

01:00:26.600 --> 01:00:29.015
What's with this guy?

01:00:32.371 --> 01:00:34.682
- What happened here?
- Head over there first.

01:00:34.682 --> 01:00:37.534
- Where's Mr. Bong? Why are you alone?
- He's over there!

01:00:52.391 --> 01:00:53.475
Get in quickly!

01:00:53.475 --> 01:00:56.052
Hurry, hurry, hurry! Fast!

01:01:02.193 --> 01:01:03.894
Piss off!

01:01:07.865 --> 01:01:09.742
Get a grip!

01:01:09.742 --> 01:01:10.951
Is he badly hurt?

01:01:10.951 --> 01:01:13.820
I don't know.
There seems to be no external injury.

01:01:14.455 --> 01:01:15.789
And breathing is normal too.

01:01:15.789 --> 01:01:17.374
It's because the Hulk was here.

01:01:17.374 --> 01:01:19.251
The Hulk?

01:01:19.251 --> 01:01:22.129
He'll be fine soon.

01:01:22.129 --> 01:01:23.631
My uncle isn't an ordinary person.

01:01:23.631 --> 01:01:26.842
Hulk or not, why is he lying there like that?

01:01:26.842 --> 01:01:29.220
Prosecutor Kang,
the video you were supposed to shoot,

01:01:29.220 --> 01:01:30.888
I'm guessing you got it done right?

01:01:30.888 --> 01:01:33.432
I did film it, but there were some variables.

01:01:33.432 --> 01:01:35.351
- Variables?
- Let's head to the practice room first.

01:01:35.351 --> 01:01:37.144
I'll explain there.

01:01:48.656 --> 01:01:50.908
- Shall we go?
- Yeah, are you okay?

01:01:50.908 --> 01:01:52.284
Yeah.

01:01:52.284 --> 01:01:53.410
Hey!

01:01:53.410 --> 01:01:55.111
What?

01:01:56.205 --> 01:01:57.790
- Where have I seen that car before?
- I don't know.

01:01:57.790 --> 01:01:59.250
Hurry, hurry, go, just go.

01:01:59.250 --> 01:02:01.242
Oh, yes.

01:02:09.635 --> 01:02:12.471
We're done here. Time to go.

01:02:12.471 --> 01:02:14.422
- Hey, it's time!
- Let's go.

01:02:23.315 --> 01:02:27.018
Boss, boss! Get a grip, boss!

01:02:27.861 --> 01:02:31.272
What the heck, hey, hey!
Chase them, you punks, hurry!

01:02:32.199 --> 01:02:34.401
Let's go, boss. Darn it!

01:02:35.828 --> 01:02:37.529
Hey, catch them!

01:02:38.330 --> 01:02:40.031
Man, this is rough.

01:02:40.031 --> 01:02:42.014
Hurry, after them!

01:02:43.210 --> 01:02:45.328
Ah, jeez...

01:02:46.505 --> 01:02:48.623
- Go, go!
- Yes.

01:02:50.801 --> 01:02:53.012
- Quick, chase them!
- What's wrong with this?

01:02:53.012 --> 01:02:54.680
- What's up with this?
- What?

01:02:54.680 --> 01:02:55.848
Something's wrong with the car.

01:02:55.848 --> 01:02:58.508
- Why won't this thing start?
- Gosh!

01:03:08.652 --> 01:03:10.687
Hurry up, you punk!

01:03:11.947 --> 01:03:13.648
Darn it!

01:03:27.713 --> 01:03:29.748
Man, this is tough.

01:03:59.080 --> 01:04:01.960
So this so-called Masked Racer showed up,

01:04:01.960 --> 01:04:05.640
and all the drugs just vanished
into thin air?

01:04:05.640 --> 01:04:07.432
- A double agent?
- You can handle it, right?

01:04:07.432 --> 01:04:09.432
Patrolling is my specialty. Don't worry.

01:04:09.432 --> 01:04:10.824
Honestly, I've always thought

01:04:10.824 --> 01:04:12.196
that police officer was suspicious.

01:04:12.196 --> 01:04:14.536
So she approached Kang Beom Ryong on purpose?

01:04:14.536 --> 01:04:15.912
I'll keep watch from the side.

01:04:15.912 --> 01:04:18.856
Do I look like an idiot
who'd lose it over something like this?

01:04:20.104 --> 01:04:21.704
Bong Jae Soon, what if...

01:04:21.704 --> 01:04:24.520
What would you do if your past turned out
completely different from what you believed?

01:04:24.520 --> 01:04:25.992
Uncle, you turned into the Hulk yesterday.

01:04:25.992 --> 01:04:27.702
Jeong Ho Myung and I are the kind of people

01:04:27.702 --> 01:04:29.928
- who could turn on each other any time, no?
- This punk, really...

01:04:29.928 --> 01:04:31.880
Beom Ryong, you're the only one I trust.

01:04:31.880 --> 01:04:33.704
If you resign voluntarily even now...

01:04:33.704 --> 01:04:35.432
Are you trying to threaten me?

01:04:35.432 --> 01:04:36.784
Gather all of our guys together.

01:04:36.784 --> 01:04:38.248
You need to take responsibility.

01:04:38.248 --> 01:04:39.400
I've already made up my mind.

01:04:39.400 --> 01:04:40.680
Where did Bulgae suddenly come from?

01:04:40.680 --> 01:04:42.440
It was Bong Jae Soon.

01:04:42.440 --> 01:04:44.872
This is definitely not a coincidence.
